WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.180
Hey YouTubers, it's Charlie. 

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:08.700
This is going to be my Arrow Episode 10 video. SO many new questions, even though we got a whole bunch of big answers.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.337
So, I'll try to answer everything as well as explain who the new characters we saw were.

00:00:12.337 --> 00:00:16.440
Thank you everyone for all the nice comments during my "CW FanTalk" appearance. 

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.980
We actually got to meet the writer of last night's Flash episode, and Emily Bett recorded a special message.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.634
So if I ever do something like that again, I'll totally let you guys know in one of my videos.

00:00:24.651 --> 00:00:26.251
Just so you can watch it.

00:00:26.251 --> 00:00:27.331
So just, careful for spoilers. 

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:32.680
I'm going to do a quick rundown of all the new storylines that they teed-up, just because those are really important.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:40.050
So we have like, character arcs that we need to talk about. We have big moments from the episode, and then we have to talk about the big, running storylines.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.100
So in present day, we have Storyline No. 1 with 'Team Brick' in the Glades.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:51.860
That's going to be part of the 'Canary Trilogy' that's happening. Brick is going to be like, the final boss that Team Arrow (or the new* Team Arrow) has to defeat.

00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:56.527
Think of him as like a final boss fight -- so they have to fight a bunch of smaller bosses before they get to him.

00:00:56.527 --> 00:01:00.380
 No. 2: We have 'Flash Back' Oliver with the China White bio-weapon.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:05.177
No. 3: There's "Team Merlyn" supposedly on the run now (or that's what they're teasing).

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.940
No. 4: Ray Palmer finishing his A.T.O.M. Suit and testing it out.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.900
And then, No. 5: Oliver, in present day, being healed by Katana &amp; Maseo. 

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:20.602
 Felicity is kind of floating around in the wind right now, but I think she's just going to bounce back and forth between Team Arrow and Ray Palmer; just like she's been [doing].

00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:22.220
Ok so here we go, Top 5 Moments:

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.900
So much to talk about in this episode.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.376
No. 5: The "New" Team Arrow.

00:01:26.376 --> 00:01:29.664
That opening scene explained everything about what you need to know about the new Team Arrow.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.300
"I thought he was green?"

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.000
"I thought he was supposed to be good?"

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:38.260
I love that everyone always asks about Diggle putting on a costume (and they stuck him in Oliver's costume).

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.080
He's worn it before. If you remember back in Season 1.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.980
 When [Oliver] needed to throw someone off his scent, he would have Diggle dress-up as the Arrow so that he could stand 

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:50.520
next to 'said person' and they would see he couldn't be the vigilante, "[...] because he's right there and I'm right here". 

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.820
And I know everyone wants to know if he's ever going to get a costume of his own. 

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.160
No, I don't think that Diggle is ever going to wear his own costume.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:58.460
I don't think he's going to be Green Lantern.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.420
I think he'll just be "Diggle"; like, he's already kind of a superhero.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:06.840
But I do think they'll have a little bit of fun with it like they did in this episode (where they stick him in other people's costumes).

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.861
So just for the next couple of episodes, it's just going to be Roy, Diggle, and Black Canary.

00:02:11.861 --> 00:02:15.121
But for the meantime, those three people are just going to be pursuing all those enforcers

00:02:15.121 --> 00:02:19.460
that got away. Until* they get to that final boss fight and have to take down Brickwell, himself.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:22.920
No. 4: Merlyn and Thea need to 'GTFO'.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:27.280
This was actually one of the more confusing parts of the episode. Merlyn said they need to, "GET OUT". 

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:31.640
Obviously because the League of Assassins is still coming for 'em. Because Oliver's death meant that

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.140
Merlyn is still marked for death.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.877
So it's really not Thea that's in danger -- it's just Merlyn -- and Merlyn wants to keep her close.

00:02:37.877 --> 00:02:42.277
There was something really important that John Barrowman said in one of the promos that they were posting last week:

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.600
"Family is more important than anything"

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:51.500
And when Thea was talking about Oliver, Merlyn said, "He's family". So, that makes me wonder if Merlyn is going to 

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.300
get involved with the Oliver-plot at some point.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.840
One of the funniest lines in the episode though is when Thea said, "I could have killed you!"

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.860
...and Merlyn smirks, and says, "It's cute that you think that would be possible."

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.440
Mostly it's just him being a badass, but you could build a lot of double-meanings in to that.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.960
But, If Oliver is coming back, if he's getting healed back to health, obviously they have some sort of special-methods inside the

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.600
League of Assassins and Katana has some special skills.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:19.000
So, maybe Merlyn also has those special skills -- which means he's almost* unkillable.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.900
 No. 3: Meet Danny Brickwell (a.k.a. "Brick" from the comics).

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:29.186
His backstory in the comics is really mysterious. Not a lot is known about him before he showed up in Star City.

00:03:29.186 --> 00:03:34.426
Yes, he is a metahuman in the comics. He has like, super-strong skin, so he's almost indestructible. 

00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:37.088
I don't* think that Arrow is going to go that direction.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.740
I think they'll just explain that he has like metal-plating in his head; something to just make him tougher.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.880
I don't think he's going to be a full-blown metahuman on Arrow (even though Arrow IS open to doing powers).

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.790
On the show he's going to be taking over The Glades, becoming like the new big crimeboss of Star City.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.180
In the comics he kind of did the same thing.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:04:00.563
So after this big event, called the "Amsterdam Avenue Disaster" (it's like the comicbook-version of the Undertaking from Season 1)

00:04:00.563 --> 00:04:04.363
Malcom Merlyn and Doctor Light just blow up a bunch of bombs all over Star City.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.960
Now that's the comics. Obviously on Arrow they did that in Season 1 with the Undertaking.

00:04:08.963 --> 00:04:13.793
Just think of him as rising from the ashes of the Undertaking, and just grabbing all the territory he could.

00:04:13.793 --> 00:04:19.620
The way he's explained in the comics is that his rise to power, isn't* tied to his abilities as a metahuman.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.440
They just put him forth as this REALLY smart criminal.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:27.320
But you can't  put  Vinnie Jones in a TV show, without letting him punch someone in the face.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.320
So there will be a lot of him fighting people.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.738
No. 2: Laurel takes the mantle of the "Black Canary".

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:37.778
I've seen a lot of questions from you guys about 'powers'. You know, how they're going to express [them]. How they're going to deal with her character.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.980
How they're going to show her, evolving, as a fighter.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:46.020
They haven't said anything about metahuman abilities. But I think them showing the 'Canary Cry' bombs on the table, kind of answers that question.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:49.571
So she's not going to get her "Canary Cry" like she has in the comics.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:57.660
This Canary Trilogy is meant to address her getting better as a hero. So she's going to get her butt kicked, a lot, in these next couple of episodes.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.060
Eventually she'll get a little bit better.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:02.420
It's the same deal with Roy. If you remember, in the beginning of the episode

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.860
when he was chasing the criminals, and they were like, "Isn't he supposed to be good?" 

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.480
Roy is going to mess a LOT of stuff up (and so is Black Canary).

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.873
So it's not like she's going to be a superhero right away.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.240
She's going to be more like, a 'cosplay'-vigilante.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.280
I think there's a little bit of confusion about that.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:21.854
Just because she gets a superhero costume, doesn't mean that the writers want you to think that she's a superhero.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:25.654
The really funny thing from behind the scenes though, is that Caity Lotz was actually talking about her

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:32.000
taking the mantle -- about Laurel taking the mantle -- she said that Katie Cassidy's wig was way better than hers.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.960
She called her "Sarah-Wig" more of like a 'Dolly Parton'-wig (which I think is kind of funny).

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:41.060
So every time I watch old episodes from Season 2 and see Black Canary, I think of Dolly Parton fighting crime.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:46.960
For those of you that are huge Sarah fans and are really sad to see her go, she will be back this season in the "Canaries" episode. 

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.220
I think it's either Episode 12 or 13

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.340
(in a flashback).

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:55.320
She also goes to a ton of conventions so you can still totally get her autograph and talk to her about how much you loved her.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:01.420
I think it's interesting though that Laurel is the one who kind of kicks everyone in the butt and says, "ARE you coming back" you know, [to] Diggle.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.280
"We have ALL these people we need to catch...we can't let them get away"

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:08.620
So she* is going to be the driving force for these next couple of episodes in catching these people.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:12.940
And that person she took down at the end of the episode: that was the person from the trial earlier.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:16.880
And, my No. 1 moment, of course: WTF? Oliver wakes up.

00:06:16.887 --> 00:06:19.962
This was like the biggest surprise of the episode, for a number of different reasons.

00:06:19.962 --> 00:06:24.722
One, that they answered the 'dead/not dead' question so fast. I thought they were going to leave that question

00:06:24.722 --> 00:06:26.042
hanging for a little bit longer.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.820
I'm glad they answered it, but now they have to answer why he's not going back right away.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:34.100
As for the Katana-thing, I'll explain this in my 'Thumbs Down' a little bit.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.740
I feel like she's a bit of a Deus Ex Machina, right now.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:42.560
I think* they had other plans for the character in the first-half of the season, but then the actress that was going to play her dropped out

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.400
[and] they had to recast her. 

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.440
So I think they had to rewrite a lot of the story.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:48.800
I think there were a lot of Katana scenes earlier on, that got written out.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:55.080
It's just, we barely spent any time with her the first half of the season...and all of a sudden, now, she's like the most important person in the world.

00:06:55.087 --> 00:06:57.520
For example, the character that played Ted Grant:

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:02.889
(Wildcat) he was cast on another show, so they might not be able to bring him back, at all, this season.

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:06.469
And originally it seemed like they had bigger plans for the Wildcat character.

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:10.460
Either way, Oliver's alive, and now we get to find out why he doesn't go back right away.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:15.373
That's going to be the most fun thing about that -- it's going to be like, 'how long is he going to sit there and stew in that cabin?'

00:07:15.373 --> 00:07:18.200
'How much longer before he let's his friends know that he's alive?'

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.773
Here's my big question for you guys:

00:07:19.773 --> 00:07:24.380
How much time do you think is going to go by, before Oliver let's his friends know that he's still alive?

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.240
There's a couple of ways that could go down.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:31.060
He could surprise everyone in like a big "hero" moment (like in a big fight with Brick or some other big villain.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:35.140
Or, two, someone else could let them know that Oliver's still alive.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:40.760
Okay, so here are the really big character arcs that I think are going to be happening (because some of the characters WILL be changing, quite a bit):

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.009
Starting off with Roy.

00:07:42.009 --> 00:07:47.240
So, Roy -- obviously, we saw him with a drink in that hand -- I think he's totally going to go alcoholic. 

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:52.108
If you remember in the comics, he became a heroine addict. I feel like that* is going to be what this storyline is.

00:07:52.108 --> 00:07:54.340
It's going to be his downward slope.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:59.340
It's even like the Laurel storyline in Season 2, where Laurel started popping pills and started drinking too much.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:02.240
I'm hoping that Laurel will actually help save him.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:07.900
It just seems like her being a recovering alcoholic, will [allow her to] recognize that happening in someone else, and she'll help them.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:15.780
Laurel of course, pretty easy to see where her character arc is going. She's going to take the mantle of the Black Canary; learn to be a superhero over 'x' amount of time. 

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:22.520
It's going to be an ongoing process. I mean Oliver is still learning to be a superhero, and he's been at it for five years longer than any of the other characters.

00:08:22.526 --> 00:08:25.165
Diggle is going to take more of a leadership role. 

00:08:25.165 --> 00:08:29.140
I mean, he's like the old man on the team now, so, naturally he has more experience than all of them.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:32.560
Felicity, kind of blowing in the wind...still waiting to see where she lands. 

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:34.880
But, I do think she'll come back and she'll start helping.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:38.981
And Ray Palmer of course, going to finish his A.T.O.M. suit and test it out.

00:08:38.981 --> 00:08:41.018
Merlyn &amp; Thea are actually pretty interesting. 

00:08:41.018 --> 00:08:46.458
There've been some pictures of her with like that 'Mystery DJ' character, so it sounds like she* might not be leaving Starling City

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.000
(regardless of what Merlyn does).

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:54.560
I'm really curious to see where their plot will intersect with Team Arrow, and the Oliver plot (like Oliver off in Nanda Parbat).

00:08:54.563 --> 00:08:56.603
"Family is more important than anything."

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.620
Just, think of that whenever you're thinking of Merlyn.

00:08:58.845 --> 00:09:00.585
And then we have Oliver in present day.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.020
Obviously he's going to  heal himself...get better...come back.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:08.520
During that CW FanTalk, one of the writers actually said that he might be having some dreams too.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.100
So we might get a lot of Oliver-dream-sequences as he's healing.

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:16.160
They also said, not all those dreams are going to be good, so he's probably going to be having some crazy nightmares.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.400
All the stunts were great. Totally Amazing.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:22.720
They really gave all the good stunts, [that] they would normally give to Stephen Amell, to Colton Haynes. 

00:09:22.723 --> 00:09:26.447
So, Colton is like the new "Stephen Amell" on the show (at least until Oliver comes back).

00:09:26.447 --> 00:09:28.047
There were a couple thumbs down I had.

00:09:28.047 --> 00:09:29.907
So first was the courtroom scenes. 

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:33.680
I feel like they don't really need to do courtroom scenes. They could have done those in the police station

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:36.220
and just saved time. They wouldn't have had to cast all those extras.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:42.200
They just wanted to set up that moment for the end, where Black Canary could take down that criminal from the courtroom scene.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.860
And then the 'Katana' plot, which I kind of mentioned.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.160
She doesn't really feel like a full character right now. 

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:50.240
It just feels like they didn't spend enough time with her in the first-half of the season.

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.080
I think a lot of that is just due to logistical problems.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:59.160
It's always interesting to see the plans producers make at the beginning of the season, and then see what finally ends up getting shot.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.500
Like what ends up turning into the actual episodes.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:06.200
All in all, great episode. Strong opener. I like the way they opened this episode, and The Flash.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:10.540
Both with people, like, screaming through the frame right as the episode starts.

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:15.680
So you have the Flash, running right through the frame, and then you have the car just running right through at the beginning of Arrow.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:19.920
So I'll be posting next week's episodes right after the episodes air. I don't have any podcasts planned

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:22.780
or anything like that. So it'll be more like my normal schedule.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.300
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:27.280
I will be posting a Q&amp;A for this on Thursday though.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:30.720
So if you have any specific questions you want me to answer, just leave them in the comments.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.680
I also saw some news about "Suicide Squad": 

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.600
Supposedly Jake Gyllenhaal has turned down the role

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:38.480
that Tom Hardy dropped out of. That was the "Rick Flag" character.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:44.080
So any of you who hated the idea of Jake Gyllenhaal in Suicide Squad -- it sounds like you won't have to worry.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:46.580
People asking about my latest Last Airbender episode: 

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:51.300
Actually, because I had to go on the CW FanTalk today, I had a little less time to get it out.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.360
So I'll just push that out as soon as possible.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.080
Right after this.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.780
And thank you again, everyone that came on and said really nice things in the chat. 

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:58.420
I saw a lot of like, 

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:02.420
"Emergency Awesome" tags, like in the CW FanCast chat. It was really cool.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:06.580
Speaking of that, if you guys want to, you can now submit fansubs on this video.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.100
All you have to do is just go into the Subs menu and you can click, "Add [subtitles/CC]"

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:11.660
You can add your native language.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.220
In case you haven't seen it yet, you can click here* for my "Flash Episode" from last night.

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:18.760
And, click here* to learn more about what's going to be happening on Arrow this season.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.060
Thank you so much for watching. So let's all high-five. 

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:22.660
I'll see you guys tonight.

